			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783535543350,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "* Root Node: The topmost node in a tree, which does not have a parent. \n  - Example: 15 is the root node.\n* Child Node: A node that is an immediate successor of another node. \n  - Example: 3 and 6 are children of 35.\n* Leaf Node (External Node): Nodes that do not have any children. \n  - Example: 1, 10, 12, 5, 7, 7 are leaf nodes.\n* Internal Node: A node with at least one child.",
			"rawText": "* Root Node: The topmost node in a tree, which does not have a parent. \n  - Example: 15 is the root node.\n* Child Node: A node that is an immediate successor of another node. \n  - Example: 3 and 6 are children of 35.\n* Leaf Node (External Node): Nodes that do not have any children. \n  - Example: 1, 10, 12, 5, 7, 7 are leaf nodes.\n* Internal Node: A node with at least one child.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "* Root Node: The topmost node in a tree, which does not have a parent. \n  - Example: 15 is the root node.\n* Child Node: A node that is an immediate successor of another node. \n  - Example: 3 and 6 are children of 35.\n* Leaf Node (External Node): Nodes that do not have any children. \n  - Example: 1, 10, 12, 5, 7, 7 are leaf nodes.\n* Internal Node: A node with at least one child.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
