		},
		{
			"id": "kEEOQGlk",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -395.4362903038365,
			"y": 802.2020800020097,
			"width": 981.8643848684737,
			"height": 150,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#e3fafc",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "ax",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1132388540,
			"version": 107,
			"versionNonce": 450465284,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783534691642,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Trees are the structural foundation of systems that naturally form hierarchies:\n\n* Operating Systems: Your computer's file system (Directories → Folders → Files).\n* Web Development: The DOM (Document Object Model) where <html> is \n  the root, and <head> / <body> are its children.\n* Routing: Network routing protocols and organizational hierarchy charts.",
			"rawText": "Trees are the structural foundation of systems that naturally form hierarchies:\n\n* Operating Systems: Your computer's file system (Directories → Folders → Files).\n* Web Development: The DOM (Document Object Model) where <html> is \n  the root, and <head> / <body> are its children.\n* Routing: Network routing protocols and organizational hierarchy charts.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Trees are the structural foundation of systems that naturally form hierarchies:\n\n* Operating Systems: Your computer's file system (Directories → Folders → Files).\n* Web Development: The DOM (Document Object Model) where <html> is \n  the root, and <head> / <body> are its children.\n* Routing: Network routing protocols and organizational hierarchy charts.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
