			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783545651177,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Definition: Each node can have at most three children (Left, Mid, Right).\nConstraint: Branching factor is restricted to 3.\nKey Examples:\n  - Ternary Search Tree: A hybrid between a Trie and a BST; efficient for string \n    searching.\n  - Ternary Heap: A variation of a binary heap where nodes have 3 children, which can \n    sometimes provide better cache performance in specific memory layouts.",
			"rawText": "Definition: Each node can have at most three children (Left, Mid, Right).\nConstraint: Branching factor is restricted to 3.\nKey Examples:\n  - Ternary Search Tree: A hybrid between a Trie and a BST; efficient for string \n    searching.\n  - Ternary Heap: A variation of a binary heap where nodes have 3 children, which can \n    sometimes provide better cache performance in specific memory layouts.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "3Q6z0wIkD-dMx4Kb3gIJg",
			"originalText": "Definition: Each node can have at most three children (Left, Mid, Right).\nConstraint: Branching factor is restricted to 3.\nKey Examples:\n  - Ternary Search Tree: A hybrid between a Trie and a BST; efficient for string \n    searching.\n  - Ternary Heap: A variation of a binary heap where nodes have 3 children, which can \n    sometimes provide better cache performance in specific memory layouts.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
